WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.961 --> 00:00:18.443
let's enroll another girl in the school," Jo said one morning.

2
00:00:18.463 --> 00:00:24.105
"Daisy needs a playmate, and another girl would improve the boys' behavior."

3
00:00:25.826 --> 00:00:27.066
Mr. Bauer nodded.

4
00:00:27.086 --> 00:00:29.548
"Do you have anyone in mind?"

5
00:00:29.848 --> 00:00:30.408
he asked.

6
00:00:32.612 --> 00:00:34.453
"Annie Harding," Jo said.

7
00:00:35.354 --> 00:00:37.955
Annie was a ten-year-old who'd lost her mother.

8
00:00:39.336 --> 00:00:41.997
Jo had run into her father in town recently.

9
00:00:42.017 --> 00:00:44.199
"Naughty Nan!"

10
00:00:44.639 --> 00:00:46.140
Mr. Bauer exclaimed.

11
00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:53.964
"That's what the boys call her," Jo said, "but I just see a girl running wild since her

12
00:00:54.004 --> 00:00:54.584
mother died.

13
00:00:55.845 --> 00:01:00.688
I was such a naughty child myself, and I remember how much my mother helped me.

14
00:01:02.432 --> 00:01:08.135
I've already talked to Nan's father—since he and Nan are visiting some friends nearby today, he's going to

15
00:01:08.195 --> 00:01:11.156
drop her off this afternoon, if that's all right."

16
00:01:12.597 --> 00:01:16.678
"As far as I'm concerned, you can bring home a dozen Nans," said Mr.

17
00:01:16.718 --> 00:01:18.579
Bauer, who loved children.

18
00:01:18.599 --> 00:01:22.421
"I doubt she'll turn out to be another troublemaker."

19
00:01:24.722 --> 00:01:25.542
Jo sighed.

20
00:01:25.562 --> 00:01:28.884
"I can never forgive myself for letting Dan go."

21
00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:35.902
When Nan arrived, she ran into the house, shouting for Daisy.

22
00:01:39.124 --> 00:01:42.426
Daisy came downstairs, pleased to see the other girl.

23
00:01:42.446 --> 00:01:49.489
"My big suitcase is coming tomorrow by train because we couldn't fit it in our carriage today," Nan

24
00:01:49.549 --> 00:01:53.371
announced. "I'm going to stay here forever!"

25
00:01:53.391 --> 00:01:55.692
"Oh my!"

26
00:01:56.864 --> 00:02:02.589
Daisy looked somewhat alarmed at that news, but she quickly recovered and remembered to be polite.

27
00:02:02.609 --> 00:02:05.811
"Do you want to play in my kitchen?"

28
00:02:07.312 --> 00:02:09.794
"No, I want to see the boys and the barn."

29
00:02:12.697 --> 00:02:16.660
Nan took off, swinging her hat by one string until it broke.

30
00:02:18.561 --> 00:02:20.743
She left her hat where it fell on the grass.

31
00:02:22.104 --> 00:02:26.388
Daisy followed Nan to the barn and found the boys sitting outside.

32
00:02:28.056 --> 00:02:30.218
"I'm here and I'm going to stay!"

33
00:02:30.618 --> 00:02:31.259
Nan said.

34
00:02:31.279 --> 00:02:37.704
"Hooray!" Tommy liked Nan because she was always ready for adventure.

35
00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:41.447
"Let's play baseball," Nan said.

36
00:02:41.467 --> 00:02:47.692
"We just finished a game," Demi said, resting against the barn wall.

37
00:02:47.712 --> 00:02:52.516
"How about a race—I bet I can beat you all," Nan said.

38
00:02:54.078 --> 00:02:56.600
Nat looked at Tommy and asked if it was true.

39
00:02:57.996 --> 00:03:01.857
"I hate to admit it, but she's really fast," Tommy said.

40
00:03:01.877 --> 00:03:09.279
"She's still a girl," Jack said, "and all girls are crybabies."

41
00:03:09.299 --> 00:03:13.360
"I never cry no matter how badly I'm hurt!"

42
00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:15.741
Nan said, sounding insulted.

43
00:03:15.761 --> 00:03:19.382
"I could make you cry in two seconds."

44
00:03:20.542 --> 00:03:23.363
Jack pointed to some plants at the edge of the field.

45
00:03:23.383 --> 00:03:27.464
"Go pick some of those stinging nettles over there."

46
00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:36.183
Nan instantly grabbed a bunch of plants with both hands and held on, despite the pain.

47
00:03:41.306 --> 00:03:45.689
After that, even Jack had to admit Nan wasn't a crybaby.

48
00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:49.231
That night at supper, Mr.

49
00:03:49.291 --> 00:03:52.332
Bauer officially welcomed Nan to Plumfield.

50
00:03:53.473 --> 00:03:58.396
He held out his hand for her to shake, but Nan kept her hands behind her back.

51
00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:01.121
"What's wrong with your hands?"

52
00:04:01.482 --> 00:04:02.603
the professor asked.

53
00:04:05.285 --> 00:04:09.229
Daisy took a deep breath and told the adults the whole story.

54
00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:13.513
"Oh, your poor hands!"

55
00:04:14.453 --> 00:04:18.377
Mr. Bauer looked at Jo, and both of them smiled slightly.

56
00:04:21.139 --> 00:04:25.884
Nan had been there only a few hours, and already she was stirring things up.

57
00:04:27.556 --> 00:04:30.818
"Do you know why I asked Nan to come stay with us?"

58
00:04:31.218 --> 00:04:32.419
Jo said to the boys.

59
00:04:32.439 --> 00:04:35.741
"To help me make gentlemen of you."

60
00:04:35.761 --> 00:04:38.702
"I hate boys!"

61
00:04:39.143 --> 00:04:40.423
Nan said fiercely.

62
00:04:40.443 --> 00:04:47.568
"I'm sorry to hear that—our boys can be quite nice when they try," Jo said.

63
00:04:49.869 --> 00:04:54.892
The boys took the hint, and for the rest of supper, they were very polite to Nan.

64
00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:01.164
The first thing Nan said the next morning was "Has my suitcase arrived?"

65
00:05:01.184 --> 00:05:05.748
"It's supposed to come sometime today," Jo said.

66
00:05:07.169 --> 00:05:10.932
Nan was disappointed but somehow managed to survive.

67
00:05:12.714 --> 00:05:15.656
Only at suppertime did Jo realize she was missing.

68
00:05:15.676 --> 00:05:21.261
"I saw her running down the drive earlier," Asia said.

69
00:05:21.281 --> 00:05:24.464
"I hope she hasn't gone home," Jo said.

70
00:05:25.936 --> 00:05:30.757
"Maybe she went to the train station to fetch her suitcase," Demi suggested.

71
00:05:30.777 --> 00:05:34.098
"She doesn't know the way," Mr.

72
00:05:34.138 --> 00:05:39.500
Bauer said, "and besides, how could she carry such a heavy load back here?"

73
00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:44.181
"Nan could probably figure out all that," Jo said.

74
00:05:45.402 --> 00:05:48.643
She couldn't help smiling even as she worried about Nan.

75
00:05:48.663 --> 00:05:53.564
"But why don't you take the carriage, Fritz, and search for her."

76
00:05:54.988 --> 00:05:55.989
"There she is!"

77
00:05:56.429 --> 00:05:59.092
shouted Rob, who was looking out the window.

78
00:06:01.954 --> 00:06:05.377
Nan was struggling up the drive with her suitcase.

79
00:06:07.739 --> 00:06:13.123
When the boys rushed out to help her, she insisted on carrying her load as far as the

80
00:06:13.203 --> 00:06:18.248
steps. Then she plopped on top of the suitcase.

81
00:06:18.268 --> 00:06:23.232
"I couldn't wait any longer for it to be delivered," she said.

82
00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:26.041
"But the station's a mile away!"

83
00:06:26.401 --> 00:06:27.141
Tommy said.

84
00:06:27.161 --> 00:06:29.882
"How did you even find it?"

85
00:06:29.902 --> 00:06:34.284
"I can always find my way," Nan said proudly.

86
00:06:34.304 --> 00:06:39.446
"I'm surprised the stationmaster let you take it," Demi said.

87
00:06:39.466 --> 00:06:45.168
"He was in the ticket office, so I just took it off the platform," Nan said.

88
00:06:47.409 --> 00:06:49.830
Jo shook her head at this new problem.

89
00:06:49.850 --> 00:06:53.792
"Go tell the stationmaster what's happened, Fritz.

90
00:06:55.164 --> 00:06:57.926
Otherwise he'll think Nan's suitcase was stolen."

91
00:06:59.627 --> 00:07:06.391
By now all the boys thought Nan was brave, and at supper she entertained them with her adventures.

92
00:07:10.274 --> 00:07:13.295
going to have your hands full with that girl," Mr.

93
00:07:13.336 --> 00:07:14.917
Bauer later said to Jo.

94
00:07:16.918 --> 00:07:20.180
Unfortunately for Jo, his prediction came true.

95
00:07:21.876 --> 00:07:26.961
Nan got into mischief, partly because she did whatever the boys dared her to do.

96
00:07:29.524 --> 00:07:35.890
But there was another side to Nan: she was generous with her toys and thought up new games

97
00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:37.191
for Daisy and Rob.

98
00:07:39.033 --> 00:07:44.458
And when the professor challenged her to do better than the boys at school, Nan beat them in

99
00:07:44.478 --> 00:07:45.660
the classroom too.
